ble.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-B\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"Q1\"\n      ],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"question\": \"Which state is most visited across all three traces, counting one visit for the initial state per string and one visit for every state entered on a step, breaking ties by lexicographically smallest state name?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"The visit counts are an aggregate over all steps of all traces; until the traces are executed and tallied under the stated counting rule, the maximum (and any tie-break) is not established.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A per-state visit tally aggregated over all three traces under the stated counting rule (initial state counted once per string; every entered state counted per step), plus identification of the maximum with the lexicographic tie-break applied if needed.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"Counting must follow the task's rule exactly: the initial state is counted for every string, and each state entered on a step is counted, aggregated across all strings.\",\n        \"Ties must be broken by lexicographically smallest state name.\",\n        \"The tally must be derived from the same admissible traces that settle Q1.\",\n        \"The task imposes no authorship or access restriction: locally derived evidence is admissible.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-C\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"Q1\"\n      ],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n  